course: dictionary
lesson: 11273
title: Wright, right, write and rite
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are old and now live mostly inside other words. A wright is an old word for a person who makes or builds things. You meet it at the end of words: playwright, shipwright and wheelwright.
explain: Look at the parts. A playwright is a person who writes plays, so the wright part tells you the maker. In a history lesson a wheelwright made wheels, and a shipwright built ships. Use the context to guess the job before you check.
explain: Wright also has a capital letter, because it is a family name. «The Wright brothers, Orville and Wilbur, are famous for the first powered flight.» Here Wright names people, not a job, so the sentence tells you who they were.
explain: Be careful: these words sound the same but are spelled differently. «"Write" (put down words), "right" (correct, or not left), "rite" (a ceremony) and "wright" (a maker, as in playwright) all sound the same.» Swap the meaning into the sentence to check.
fact: A wright is an old word for a maker, used now mostly at the end of words.
fact: A playwright is a person who writes plays, and it is spelled wright, not «playwrite».
fact: A wheelwright makes wheels, and a shipwright builds ships.
fact: Wright is also a common family name: Orville and Wilbur Wright were the brothers who flew the first powered aeroplane.
fact: «On 17 December 1903 the Wright brothers made the first powered, controlled flight in an aeroplane; it lasted 12 seconds.»
exercise: In English lessons, what is a playwright? | A person who sells plays | A plane that flies in a circle | A wooden box used on the stage | *A person who writes plays
exercise: A wheelwright is a person who does what? | Sells cars | Drives trains | Sings songs | *Makes wheels
exercise: «"Write", "right", "rite" and "wright" all sound the same.» Which one means a maker, as in playwright? | right | write | rite | *wright
test: On what date did the Wright brothers make the first powered, controlled flight? | *17 December 1903 | 17 December 1885 | 1 January 1886 | 12 December 1903
test: Which word means a person who builds ships? | Playwright | *Shipwright | Rite | Right
exam: Why does Wright start with a capital letter in «The Wright brothers flew in 1903»? | It is the name of a place | It means a ceremony | *It is a family name | It is a job title
